          "explanation": "Critics note that even Rand's lone genius relies on inherited knowledge: manuscripts stolen from the Scholars and a tunnel built in the Unmentionable Times. That supports the argument that discovery is cumulative. Rand would reply that inheritance only supplies materials -- the thinking itself still happens in one mind. The other options invent plot events that don't occur.",
