          "explanation": "The Unspeakable Word is \"I\" -- which the narrator also names \"ego.\" The society's entire moral order rests on the idea that the individual exists only as part of the collective. A person who can say \"I\" can think, prefer, and choose on his own, which makes the Councils' authority illegitimate. \"Freedom\" is a tempting answer, but Rand's point is deeper: freedom is impossible without a self to be free.",
